//RS 
//RS // Runtime symbols are not JavaScript property lookups.  This closed table is
//RS // the Web linkage boundary: every accepted target is a local identifier or an
//RS // explicit imported expression (such as `jetDom.webStreamCommit`), while a new
//RS // or target-inapplicable symbol fails emission instead of becoming ambient
//RS // runtime dispatch.
//RS // Namespaced Prelude symbols are admitted only when the canonical Web kernel
//RS // has an explicit local alias.  The App builder uses the same rule: its
//RS // checked chain is recorded by the browser adapter, while `jet_app_graph`
//RS // remains the compiler-owned route authority.
